  "question": {
    "text": "A box contains&nbsp;<math><mn>9</mn></math> slips bearing numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1,</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>1,</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>3,</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>. An experiment consists of drawing a slip from this box and replacing it back in the box after noting the number. This experiment is repeated <math><mn>9</mn></math> times. These <math><mn>9</mn></math> numbers are now chosen as elements of a&nbsp;<math><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>3</mn></math> matrix, then the probability that the matrix is skew symmetric is",
    "image": null
  },
